  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Product Lookups",
      "description": "Lookup tables for product classification.\n\n**Categories** (`product_category`) are a nested tree (`parent` / `children`) used by stock and plan. Other lookups (`class`, `range`, `unit`) remain flat `{id, name}` lists.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List classes",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/product/class/",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["product", "class", ""]
            },
            "description": "GET product class lookup list."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List categories",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/product/category/",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["product", "category", ""],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "parent_id",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "Optional. Omit for full tree from roots. Set to a category id for that parent's children (still nested). Use `0` or `null` for roots only.",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "### List categories\n\n`GET /product/category/`\n\nReturns the product category tree from `product_category` (legacy `tblcategories`). Each node includes classification flags, path, auto-code fields, and a nested `children[]` array — used by stock and plan UIs to pick a category without flattening the hierarchy.\n\nExample: root **Cased Items** (`127`) contains child **Catering Bulk** (`129`) under `children`.\n\n#### Query parameters\n\n| Param | Required | Notes |\n|-------|----------|-------|\n| `parent_id` | No | Omit → full forest from roots. Integer id → that parent's direct children (each still nested). `0` or `null` → roots only. Invalid non-integer → 400. |\n\n#### Request body\n\n**None**.\n\n#### Response body\n\nMessage: `Product categories fetched successfully.`\n\n`data` is an array of category nodes:\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|-------|--------|\n| `id` | Category PK (legacy id) |\n| `name` | Display name |\n| `parent_id` | Parent category id, or `null` for roots |\n| `is_default` | Default category flag |\n| `is_container` | Legacy container marker |\n| `purchase_unit_id` | Default purchase unit FK |\n| `multiplier` | Qty multiplier (string or `null`) |\n| `path` | Denormalized path text |\n| `path_nodes` | Denormalized id path |\n| `code_generator` / `code_generator_path` | Auto-code templates |\n| `last_increment_auto_code` | Last auto-code sequence |\n| `item_flag` | Item type flag (SmallInt; default `-1`) |\n| `is_range` / `is_resource` / `is_container_flag` / `is_other` | Type flags |\n| `is_locked` / `is_locked_assigned` / `is_locked_path` | Lock flags |\n| `remarks` | Notes |\n| `children` | Nested child category nodes (same shape) |\n\n#### Status codes\n\n| Code | When |\n|------|------|\n| 200 | Tree returned |\n| 400 | `parent_id` present but not an integer |"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List categories by parent",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/product/category/?parent_id=127",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["product", "category", ""],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "parent_id",
                  "value": "127",
                  "description": "Parent category id. Returns that parent's children with nested `children[]`."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "### List categories by parent\n\n`GET /product/category/?parent_id=:id`\n\nSame payload shape as **List categories**, scoped to one parent's children. Use when a UI drills into a node (e.g. open **Cased Items** → load its children only).\n\n#### Query parameters\n\n| Param | Required | Notes |\n|-------|----------|-------|\n| `parent_id` | Yes (for this request) | Integer category id. `0` / `null` → roots. |\n\n#### Request body\n\n**None**.\n\n#### Response body\n\nSame nested node shape as **List categories**. Message: `Product categories fetched successfully.` Empty array if the parent has no children or the id is unknown.\n\n#### Status codes\n\n| Code | When |\n|------|------|\n| 200 | Children returned (may be empty) |\n| 400 | `parent_id` not an integer |"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List ranges",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/product/range/",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["product", "range", ""]
            },
            "description": "GET product range lookup list."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List units",
          "request": {
